Add HTF OPENING_DRIVE_CONT paper telemetry validation

Root cause:
PR #604 classified `OPENING_DRIVE_CONT` as `READY_FOR_PAPER_RETEST`, but the replay used spot-scaled proxy option P&L. The next required step is paper-only validation using actual option quote evidence.

Scope:
This PR adds paper telemetry for `HTF_OPENING_DRIVE_CONT`. It does not enable live orders, does not weaken gates, and does not promote the strategy to live.

What changed:

* Added `core/htf_paper_telemetry.py`.
* Added paper candidate logging to `runtime/paper/htf_opening_drive_candidates.jsonl`.
* Added paper exit logging to `runtime/paper/htf_opening_drive_exits.jsonl`.
* Added `scripts/summarize_htf_opening_drive_paper.py`.
* Added `docs/strategy_research/htf_opening_drive_paper_validation_plan.md`.
* Moved telemetry capture to `TradeBuilder.build_with_trace` so both accepted candidates and hard-rejected contexts can be logged.
* Hooked paper exit outcome tracking through `core/paper_exit_outcome.py`.
* Removed the older hook from `core/opportunity_engine.py`.

Safety:

* Telemetry only runs when `PAPER_TELEMETRY_ENABLED` is enabled.
* Telemetry only runs in `execution_mode == "PAPER"`.
* LIVE mode is blocked from telemetry writes.
* Non-HTF strategies are excluded.
* Fallback/advisory/stale candidates remain non-executable.
* Telemetry write failures do not break `TradeBuilder`.
* No broker/live order path was touched.
* No execution gate was weakened.
* No strategy entry logic was changed.

Tests:

* `pytest tests/strategy_truth/test_htf_strategy_truth.py -q`
* `pytest tests -q`

Result:

* HTF paper telemetry suite: 19 passed.
* Full suite: 4722 passed, 0 failed, 1 deselected.

Expected classification after merge:
`OPENING_DRIVE_CONT = PAPER_VALIDATION_ACTIVE`

Not live-ready.
